WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,797
Cloud IAM is not only about employees signing into a console.

2
00:00:03,797 --> 00:00:05,733
Workloads also need identity.

3
00:00:05,733 --> 00:00:08,338
CI/CD pipelines deploy infrastructure.

4
00:00:08,338 --> 00:00:10,125
Containers call cloud APIs.

5
00:00:10,125 --> 00:00:12,880
Virtual machines retrieve configuration.

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,337
Serverless functions process events.

7
00:00:15,337 --> 00:00:18,910
Kubernetes workloads read secrets or publish messages.

8
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:28,961
Applications use service accounts, managed identities, workload identities, tokens, or deployment roles to perform tasks without a human clicking a button.

9
00:00:28,961 --> 00:00:32,758
Non-human identities often create the largest blind spots.

10
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:39,458
A shared service account may be used by several applications, so no one knows which system caused an action.

11
00:00:39,458 --> 00:00:44,744
A deployment role may be overpowered because it was created to make automation easy.

12
00:00:44,744 --> 00:00:49,062
A leaked access key may remain active because no owner is tracking it.

13
00:00:49,062 --> 00:00:54,199
A workload in development may accidentally have access to production resources.

14
00:00:54,199 --> 00:00:58,369
These problems are not exotic; they are normal engineering drift.

15
00:00:58,369 --> 00:01:11,249
Safer patterns include workload identity federation, managed identities, short-lived credentials, narrowly scoped deployment roles, environment separation, secret rotation, and clear ownership.

16
00:01:11,249 --> 00:01:18,545
A build pipeline should have the permissions needed to deploy its application, not broad rights across the account.

17
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:24,203
A serverless function should read the specific data it needs, not every storage resource.

18
00:01:24,203 --> 00:01:29,787
A Kubernetes workload should not share one powerful identity with unrelated workloads.

19
00:01:29,787 --> 00:01:31,573
Auditability is essential.

20
00:01:31,573 --> 00:01:40,210
Automation should leave a clear trail of which principal acted, which pipeline or workload used it, what changed, and who owns the system.

21
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:50,111
When a production change happens, responders should not have to guess whether it came from a user, a deployment tool, a managed identity, or a compromised key.

22
00:01:50,111 --> 00:01:56,067
Workload identity hardening is how cloud teams make automation fast without making it opaque.

23
00:01:56,067 --> 00:01:59,269
Environment separation is a practical guardrail.

24
00:01:59,269 --> 00:02:05,374
A development pipeline should not normally deploy to production unless that is its explicit job.

25
00:02:05,374 --> 00:02:09,096
A test service account should not read production secrets.

26
00:02:09,096 --> 00:02:14,456
A serverless function in one application should not write to another team's storage.

27
00:02:14,456 --> 00:02:19,891
These boundaries make mistakes easier to contain and ownership easier to understand.

28
00:02:19,891 --> 00:02:24,358
Workload identity design should be part of application architecture.

29
00:02:24,358 --> 00:02:32,771
When a new service is created, teams should ask which cloud APIs it needs, which resources it can touch, how credentials are delivered,

30
00:02:32,771 --> 00:02:38,429
who owns the identity, how logs identify its actions, and how access will be removed later.

31
00:02:38,429 --> 00:02:46,098
Answering those questions early is far cheaper than cleaning up an overpowered service account after production launch.

32
00:02:46,098 --> 00:02:50,341
Automation should have the same review discipline as human access.

33
00:02:50,341 --> 00:02:58,233
If a pipeline is allowed to create networks, assign roles, or deploy privileged functions, reviewers should understand why.

34
00:02:58,233 --> 00:03:02,328
The fact that a principal is non-human does not make it lower risk.

35
00:03:02,328 --> 00:03:08,879
In many cloud environments, workload identities are among the most powerful identities in the account.
